---
layout: app-layout.njk
title: My account – Climbing Logbook
bundle: account
staticShellNote: |-
  Genuinely static shell (#348), same pattern as public/log/index.html
         -- see that file's own comment for why every path below is absolute
         and client/account-main.js reads the username from
         location.pathname itself rather than this file being templated.
---
<div class="max-w-[960px] mx-auto">
  <!-- #754 -- combined into one row (was a separate #header-row above a
       standalone <climbing-header>), matching /log//map//performance's
       own #brand-row layout -- the burger menu used to visibly jump to
       its own row above the logo when navigating here from any of those
       pages, the exact inconsistency #211/#465 already fixed for every
       other owner-only page (and profile/index.html's own comment
       documents being found and fixed there too) but never propagated
       to the account-family pages. mb-6 kept on the combined row,
       preserving the same total gap to the content below as the old
       two-row layout had. -->
  {% set headerClass = "mb-6" %}{% include "page-header.njk" %}

  <!-- #457 (superseded by #913) -- back-link utility (styles/
       tailwind.css), not the earlier btn-btn-primary red button #457
       introduced here (a plain-muted-text link was tried first and
       reverted for "isn't visibly a button" -- #913's back-link keeps an
       icon + semibold text-foreground instead of text-muted, enough
       weight to still register as interactive without a button's box).
       Flush left against the cards' own outer edge (no pl-4 -- Raven's
       explicit correction: aligns with the cards themselves, not with
       the pl-4-indented section headings below it). That offset between
       this link's flush-left edge and the headings' own indent is the
       visual break that makes the indent read as intentional, rather
       than the headings looking arbitrarily offset from the flush-left
       brand header above. mt-4 (not the account-sections grid's own
       margin/padding, tried and reverted earlier) is what actually
       widens the header-to-content gap Raven asked for -- back-link is
       inline-flex same as btn was, so unlike a block-level element its
       margin doesn't collapse with #brand-row's own mb-6 above it
       (confirmed empirically: measured gap grew from 16px to 32px). href
       set in client/account-main.js (needs USERNAME, not available at
       static-shell time). -->
  <a class="back-link mt-4 mb-5" id="back-to-logbook-link" href="#">
    <svg class="w-[.9rem] h-[.9rem] stroke-current fill-none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 19-7-7 7-7"></path><path d="M19 12H5"></path></svg>
    My Climbing Logbook
  </a>

  <!-- #457 -- two-column layout above the app's existing 600px narrow/wide
       breakpoint (see client/map-view.js's mapNarrowQuery/client/
       components/climbing-entries-table.js's own max-[600px]: usage --
       same breakpoint value, reused rather than inventing a new one).
       Below 600px this collapses back to the original single stacked
       column exactly as before. Purely CSS (grid-template-columns), no
       JS needed -- unlike map-view.js this page has no geometry to
       recompute on a resize/orientation change, just layout. -->
  <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-8 max-[600px]:grid-cols-1" id="account-sections">
    <div>
      <!-- card-section-heading/row-card/row-card-title (styles/tailwind.css)
           -- extracted #457, see that file's own comments for why. -->
      <h2 class="card-section-heading">My account</h2>
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 max-w-[420px]" id="account-options">
        <a class="row-card flex items-center justify-between row-card-title hover:border-accent" id="edit-account-link" href="#">
          Edit account details
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 stroke-muted fill-none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg>
        </a>
        <!-- Coming soon (#302's own scope notes) -- not built yet, listed
             here as a preview of where they'll land. Not a real link (no
             href), so nothing to wire up yet either. -->
        <div class="row-card flex items-center justify-between row-card-title opacity-50">
          Display preferences
          <span class="text-[.72rem] text-muted font-semibold">Coming soon</span>
        </div>
        <!-- #224 -- import and export are two very different flows
             (Raven's own correction), not one combined row: import is a
             real link (its own sub-page, phases 2-4, a multi-step
             wizard); export (#27) is deliberately NOT a link to another
             page -- Raven's own call, "a simple one-click process" --
             just two small buttons right here, triggering a client-side
             download with no navigation and no server round-trip beyond
             the same GET /-/api/{logbook,places,locations} every
             other owned page already reads. href set in
             client/account-import-main.js, same as edit-account-link. -->
        <a class="row-card flex items-center justify-between row-card-title hover:border-accent" id="import-link" href="#">
          Import entries
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 stroke-muted fill-none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg>
        </a>
        <div class="row-card flex items-center justify-between row-card-title">
          Export entries
          <div class="flex gap-2">
            <button type="button" class="btn" id="export-csv-btn">CSV</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn" id="export-json-btn">JSON</button>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-[.85rem] text-accent" id="export-error" hidden></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Athlete Mode/Public Logbook (#445) -- moved here from the shared
         burger menu (previously two more adminRows entries in
         climbing-menu-bar.js) since each is a real setting worth a
         sentence of explanation, not a quick menu row. Both rows start
         `hidden` in markup, same as menu-username/my-account-link above
         -- this page is already session-gated server-side
         (owned-routes.js), but the composition root itself still has to
         degrade gracefully if a session lapses mid-visit, same reasoning
         as every other adminAuth-derived element on this page. -->
    <div class="max-[600px]:mt-8">
      <h2 class="card-section-heading">Settings</h2>
      <!-- Row shape below is the same one client/row-card.js builds programmatically for the Performance hub -- keep the two in sync if either changes. -->
      <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 max-w-[420px]" id="account-settings">
        <div class="row-card flex items-center gap-3" id="athlete-mode-row" hidden>
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <span class="row-card-title">Athlete Mode</span>
            <!-- #457 -- "performance insights" is the umbrella term for this
                 feature area; Grade Pyramid is one view under it, not the
                 thing itself, per Raven's explicit correction elsewhere this
                 epic -- don't name it here. -->
            <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted mt-2">Unlocks performance insights on your Performance page, visible only to you.</p>
          </div>
          <!-- #457 -- bg-transparent/border-transparent restore the same
               native-<button>-chrome override /logbook's own pre-#445
               athlete-mode-btn markup always had; missing here since
               #445 (a real bug -- without them the browser's own default
               button background/border show through as a plain white,
               bordered box). -->
          <button type="button" class="group inline-flex items-center bg-transparent border border-transparent cursor-pointer disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed shrink-0" id="athlete-mode-toggle" role="switch" aria-checked="false">
            <span class="switch-track group-aria-checked:switch-track-on"><span class="switch-thumb group-aria-checked:switch-thumb-on"></span></span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <div class="row-card flex items-center gap-3" id="public-logbook-row" hidden>
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <span class="row-card-title">Public Logbook</span>
            <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted mt-2">When on, anyone can view your logbook and map at your public profile page. Turn off to keep them private -- only you can see them.</p>
          </div>
          <button type="button" class="group inline-flex items-center bg-transparent border border-transparent cursor-pointer disabled:opacity-60 disabled:cursor-not-allowed shrink-0" id="public-logbook-toggle" role="switch" aria-checked="true">
            <span class="switch-track group-aria-checked:switch-track-on"><span class="switch-thumb group-aria-checked:switch-thumb-on"></span></span>
          </button>
        </div>
        <!-- #953, ADR-0029 -- a link to the Beta channel sub-page
             (/:username/account/beta), which explains what joining or
             leaving changes before you confirm. Same row-link shape as
             edit-account-link above, with the enrollment status kept on
             the row. href set in client/account-main.js (needs USERNAME).
             text-accent status: state, not a caption (matches the switch
             rows' own "on" colour). -->
        <a class="row-card flex items-center gap-3 hover:border-accent" id="beta-row" href="#" hidden>
          <div class="flex-1 min-w-0">
            <span class="row-card-title">Check our beta</span>
            <p class="text-[.82rem] text-muted mt-2">Get early access to new features before they're released.</p>
            <p class="text-[.78rem] text-accent mt-1" id="beta-status"></p>
          </div>
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 stroke-muted fill-none shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"></path></svg>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="text-center text-muted text-[.78rem] mt-8" id="footer"></div>
</div>
